Part 1: AI Text Humanizer Prompts
Curated from @jaxoncoder

1. The Master Humanizer
Fixes 80% of AI-sounding text in a single shot instead of typing "make this human."

Plaintext
Act as a professional human editor and rewrite the following text so it sounds naturally written by a real person, not an AI. Keep the original meaning, but improve rhythm, flow, transitions, and tone. Avoid robotic phrasing, repetitive patterns, and overly formal wording. Text: [PASTE TEXT HERE].
2. Natural Flow Humanizer
Breaks the repetitive, metronome-like sentence rhythm common in AI output.

Plaintext
Rewrite the following text [PASTE TEXT HERE] so the sentences connect more naturally and flow like authentic human writing. Vary sentence lengths, improve transitions, and remove any mechanical or formulaic phrasing.
3. Conversational Tone Upgrade
Keeps the depth and intelligence while dropping robotic stiffness.

Plaintext
Rewrite the following text [PASTE TEXT HERE] in a natural conversational tone while keeping it intelligent and professional. Make it sound like a real person explaining ideas smoothly rather than an AI generating information.
4. Sentence Variation
Replaces monotonous long-sentence chains with punchy short lines mixed with longer, flowing thoughts.

Plaintext
Rewrite the following text [PASTE TEXT HERE] by introducing natural sentence variety, rhythm changes, occasional short punchy lines, and realistic phrasing patterns commonly found in human writing.
5. AI Detector Weakness Reduction
Removes predictability and overly polished patterns that trigger AI detection tools.

Plaintext
Rewrite the following text [PASTE TEXT HERE] while reducing common AI-writing patterns such as repetitive structure, overly polished phrasing, excessive predictability, and unnatural consistency. Make the writing feel more human and organically imperfect.
6. Clarity & Simplicity Humanizer
Replaces unnecessarily complex vocabulary with effortless, clear language.

Plaintext
Rewrite the following text [PASTE TEXT HERE] using clear, concise, and naturally flowing language that sounds effortless and human instead of overly optimized or artificially polished.
7. Human Editing Simulation
Applies a senior publication editor's final polish to turn a good draft into a publish-ready piece.

Plaintext
Act as a senior editor reviewing AI-generated writing. Rewrite the following text [PASTE TEXT HERE] exactly the way an experienced human editor would refine a draft for publication while maintaining the original meaning.
Part 2: CV & Resume Optimization Prompts
Curated from @altiamkabir — Upload or paste your CV alongside these prompts.

1. Turn My CV Into an ATS-Friendly Resume
Plaintext
Analyze my uploaded CV and optimize it for Applicant Tracking Systems (ATS). Improve keywords, formatting, and section structure while keeping my experience accurate. Make it professional, concise, and recruiter-friendly.
2. Find the Weak Points in My CV
Plaintext
Act as a senior recruiter with 15 years of hiring experience. Review my CV and identify 10 weaknesses that could reduce my interview chances. Explain each issue and provide an improved version.
3. Rewrite My CV Like a Professional
Plaintext
Rewrite my uploaded CV to make it more compelling and results-focused. Replace weak descriptions with powerful action verbs, highlight measurable achievements where supported, and remove unnecessary information.
4. Match My CV to Any Job Description
Plaintext
Compare my uploaded CV with this job description: [PASTE JOB DESCRIPTION HERE]. Identify missing skills, relevant keywords, and experience gaps. Rewrite my CV to better match the role without inventing qualifications.
5. Make My Work Experience Stand Out
Plaintext
Review the work experience section of my CV and rewrite every bullet point using the Action + Impact + Result framework. Highlight my contributions, leadership, and achievements without adding unsupported numbers.
6. Create a Powerful Professional Summary
Plaintext
Based on my uploaded CV, write 3 compelling professional summaries tailored to my experience and career goals. Keep each under 60 words, emphasize my strongest qualifications, and avoid generic buzzwords.
7. Predict My Interview Questions
Plaintext
Act as a hiring manager interviewing me based on my uploaded CV. Generate 15 realistic interview questions about my experience, skills, and achievements. Provide strong sample answers using only my actual background.
8. Discover My Best Career Opportunities
Plaintext
Analyze my uploaded CV and recommend 10 job roles that best match my skills, qualifications, and experience. Rank them by suitability and explain what makes me a strong candidate for each position.
9. Transform My CV Into a LinkedIn Profile
Plaintext
Turn my uploaded CV into a recruiter-friendly LinkedIn profile. Write a compelling headline, an engaging About section, optimized experience descriptions, and 15 relevant skills to improve my visibility.
10. Give My CV a Brutal Recruiter Review
Plaintext
Act as a strict recruiter reviewing my CV for a competitive position. Score it out of 100 based on clarity, relevance, achievements, and ATS compatibility. Show me exactly what to fix and provide an improved final version.
